208	Mexican Chicken Fajitas with Brown Rice	A high-protein, flavorful Mexican dish combining seasoned chicken fajitas with wholesome brown rice, perfect for muscle gain.	["muscle_gain"]	["muscle_gain", "high_protein", "mexican", "meal_prep_friendly"]	["high-protein"]	["lunch", "dinner", "snack", "breakfast"]	["Cook the brown rice: In a pot, bring 555ml (triple the dry weight) of water to a boil. Add the brown rice, reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 30 minutes or until the rice is tender and has absorbed the water. Keep warm.", "In a large bowl, combine sliced chicken breast, lime juice, minced garlic, cumin, chili powder, paprika, salt, and black pepper. Mix well to coat the chicken evenly.", "Heat 15g of olive oil in a large pan over medium-high heat. Add the marinated chicken slices and cook for 5-7 minutes, turning occasionally, until fully cooked and slightly charred. Remove the chicken from the pan and set aside.", "In the same pan, add the remaining 15g of olive oil. Add sliced bell pepper and onion, and saut\\u00e9 for 5 minutes until the vegetables are tender and slightly caramelized.", "Return the cooked chicken to the pan with the vegetables, stir to combine, and cook for an additional 2 minutes to heat through.", "Serve the chicken fajitas hot over the cooked brown rice. Optionally, garnish with fresh cilantro or a squeeze of lime."]	mexican	40	0	medium	2	{"calories": 780.0, "protein_g": 61.0, "carbs_g": 85.0, "fat_g": 22.0, "fiber_g": 10.0}	\N	\N	[-0.01731063798069954, -0.03963787481188774, -0.005314669571816921, -0.004316411446779966, -0.025082990527153015, -0.04724150896072388, 0.049896031618118286, 0.038175638765096664, -0.0069287545047700405, -0.003782132640480995, -0.01454363577067852, -0.048951201140880585, -0.0075080255046486855, 0.0356111004948616, -0.009138981811702251, 0.03878302872180939, 0.0013595994096249342, 0.0011156587861478329, -0.023598257452249527, -0.013835012912750244, 0.006658803205937147, -0.010241284035146236, -0.01535